POSIX delegated errors and pathname conversion

Run python3 -B developer/debug/test/crt/posixc/native_errors_host.py.

The gate executes the actual rename, remove and rmdir bodies plus their DOS
error mapper under ASan/UBSan. The fallback executes stdc's actual mapper with
the actual DOS error constants. The modeled delegate has separate error state;
cleanup deliberately clobbers errno and IoErr. Checks cover mapping, conversion
failure, allocation failure and preserved source names across shared-buffer
reuse. rmdir must perform exactly one pathname conversion through remove,
including success and delegated failure. POSIXC maps a full volume, a protected
volume/object, a nonempty directory and a link nesting failure to its own POSIX
codes. Unknown native errors retain stdc's encoded fallback.

This does not qualify filesystem handlers, concurrent namespace mutation,
directory-only deletion or final-link semantics. In particular, rmdir's
directory-type restriction requires separate implementation and runtime proof.
